# Auto-activate the daedalus dev shell (flake.nix) on entry.
#
# WHY: under a Nix-store Python interpreter the ELF loader is the Nix glibc
# loader, which does NOT search the host FHS library path
# (/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu), so the science stack's binary wheels (numpy,
# scipy, ...) cannot find libstdc++.so.6 (the gcc runtime) or libz.so.1 at
# import time. The flake's dev shell sets a narrow, Nix-store, ABI-matched
# LD_LIBRARY_PATH (zlib + gcc runtime) that fixes exactly this. direnv exports
# that environment the moment you cd in, so `uv run python -c "import scipy"`
# works with zero manual steps.
#
# SETUP (one time): `cp .envrc.defaults .envrc && direnv allow`. Needs
# direnv >= 2.30 for the built-in `use flake`.
#
# IF DIRENV IS DISABLED: run `nix develop` by hand to enter the same shell.
use flake
